A. Final abstract (project description)
V12 Engines_IBM Z Datathon 2026 Project · Event code: SSF2026
V12 Engines is an order-time delivery-delay early-warning engine for global HIV supply chains (antiretroviral medicines and HIV test kits), running on IBM LinuxONE. 
When an order is placed, two Snap ML boosted-tree models predict the probability of a late delivery and the estimated days late. IBM Granite turns the model's top drivers into a plain-language explanation and a recommended action matched to the remaining runway (long, medium, or short). 
A logistics officer reviews each alert (Acknowledge, Take action, Dismiss), and that log is the audit trail. The models are trained on 10,324 USAID/PEPFAR shipments from 2006–2015, trained on shipments through 2013 and evaluated on 2014–2015. The demo is a replay of historical data, not a live 2026 feed; in deployment the models retrain on current data. Predicted days late is an estimate, and a human always decides.
